{
    "background_story": "In the slow-paced world of freshwater mollusks, Milan the Anodonta snail was a gentle giant. Living in the tranquil depths of a European lake, Milan spent his days filtering algae and small organisms from the water. His shell, a beautiful swirling pattern of browns and tans, protected him from predators and provided a cozy home. Milan's life was one of quiet contentment, as he slowly made his way across the lake floor, leaving behind a trail of cleaned water. Despite his sluggish pace, Milan played a vital role in maintaining the lake's ecosystem, and his species had been doing so for millennia. As the seasons passed, Milan grew old and wise, his shell a testament to the enduring power of patience and persistence.",
